<title>CANADA: WCE canola/grain pre-opening calls.</title>
<headline>WCE canola/grain pre-opening calls.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>WCE canola and grain futures pre-opening call as of 0833 CDT.</p>
<p>CANOLA - C$1.00 to C$2.00 a tonne higher on CBOT soybean calls, short covering on oversold sentiments ahead of the U.S. long weekend. July WCE futures crush margin fell to -3.74 Wednesday from +0.03 Monday. Canada's dollar opened down at C$1.3778 to the U.S. dollar, fell to 82.96 yen, fell to 1.2727 marks.</p>
<p>FLAXSEED - Steady to C$0.50 up on spill over support.</p>
<p>WESTERN BARLEY - Steady to C$0.50 higher on CBOT corn calls.</p>
<p>FEED WHEAT - Steady to C$0.50 up on spill over support.</p>
<p>PEAS - Steady.</p>
<p>OATS - Steady.</p>
<p>(All values in Canadian dollars/tonne except peas, oats)</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
